Group 3 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)
 Member 1 (Senior Pediatric Nephrologist (Lead)): Offers overarching guidance on nephrology, taking into account insights from the IAT and DET to formulate the final management plan for the child.
 Member 2 (Pediatric Surgeon): Collaborates with the nephrology team to determine if surgical intervention for correcting vesicoureteral reflux is necessary based on the diagnostic findings and overall condition of the patient.
 Member 3 (Child Psychologist): Focuses on the psychological impacts of recurrent health issues on a young child, advising on how to support the patient and family during ongoing treatment and potential surgical interventions.

